Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.22.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.22.0 reworks the floating shell interaction to the Stheno-style gesture UX the user asked for. The window now opens centered on screen instead of docked top-right. The bottom status bar joins the title bar as a move handle, so the window can be dragged from the bottom edge. The bottom-right grip resize is now aspect-ratio locked: the ratio is captured at gesture start and the pan translation is projected onto the bottom-right/top-left diagonal to produce a single scale delta - dragging toward the upper-left shrinks, toward the lower-right grows, and height is always derived from width (newH = newW / AR) so content never distorts. Clamping keeps a 150 pt minimum and keeps the window on screen while preserving the ratio (width is re-derived from clamped height). The 0.20.0 mis-touch rollback for fast vertical home swipes is kept unchanged in behavior. No new config keys, cfgVersion stays 19. 0.21.0 (unchanged here) added the C bridge surface and Swift facade skeleton and validated the Swift toolchain.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
